numpy: method and getset signatures that match how CPython calls them.

wasm checks the type of every indirect call, so a C method, getter or
setter whose definition doesn't match its calling convention traps and
kills the interpreter, where native platforms ignore the extra argument.
copy.copy(np.float64(1)) and arr.dtype = ... both trapped. Adds the
missing unused parameters, and fixes the METH_* flags of
_get_castingimpl (takes no keywords) and printf_float_g (takes them).
Found by numpy's test suite and a scan of the method and getset tables.
Used by toolchain/recipes.toml.

